meta {
  name: Admin
  seq: 5
}

docs {
  Platform operator APIs. Use Bearer {{adminToken}} (or {{token}} after Admin Login).

  Session:
  - POST /v1/auth/logout (Admin Logout — revokes JWT, clears tokens)

  Users:
  - GET   /v1/admin/users              (list + filter by plan/status/email)
  - GET   /v1/admin/users/:id
  - PATCH /v1/admin/users/:id          (status, orgs_enabled, early_bird_live grant/revoke)
  - PUT  /v1/admin/users/:id/plan      (plan)
  - PATCH enable / disable org creation (orgs_enabled true/false)
  - PUT   /v1/admin/users/:id/plan

  Organizations (E4):
  - GET   /v1/admin/orgs               (?page, limit, status, name)
  - GET   /v1/admin/orgs/:id
  - PATCH /v1/admin/orgs/:id           (status active/suspended, seat_limit)
  - GET   /v1/admin/orgs/:id/members

  Platform settings (Phase 6 — Paper Trading market data provider):
  - GET /v1/admin/settings/market-data-provider  (current provider + available options)
  - PUT /v1/admin/settings/market-data-provider  ({"provider": "signal"|"fyers"})
  Runtime-configurable — no server restart needed. Backed by a generic
  `platform_settings` key-value table (migration 037); the background
  SnapshotJob re-reads this setting on every sweep.

  FYERS connection (market-data-only, never order placement — single
  platform-wide connection, admin-managed via this API + the admin
  dashboard's Platform Settings page, not per-user):
  - GET /v1/admin/fyers/status   (connected?, pin_set?, token expiry)
  - GET /v1/admin/fyers/connect  (returns a FYERS OAuth login redirect_url)
  - PUT /v1/admin/fyers/pin      ({"pin": "1234"} — needed for silent refresh)
  - GET /v1/admin/fyers/callback is PUBLIC (FYERS redirects the browser here
    directly after login) — not called from this collection.
  See fyers-connect.bru docs for the full flow and what's verified vs.
  best-effort in the underlying FYERS API integration.

  Market profiles & instruments (Phase 7 — curated, not admin-created):
  - GET   /v1/admin/market-profiles          (list, active first)
  - PATCH /v1/admin/market-profiles/:code    (base_currency/timezone/active
    only — name/code are fixed identity, not accepted by this endpoint)
  - GET    /v1/admin/instruments             (?market_profile=<code>)
  - POST   /v1/admin/instruments             (add a symbol)
  - PATCH  /v1/admin/instruments/:id         (name/instrument_type/tick_size/
    lot_size/active)
  - DELETE /v1/admin/instruments/:id
  There is deliberately no POST for market-profiles — profiles are seeded via
  migration, not created ad hoc through the API.

  Also: GET /v1/me (admin profile)
}
